          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Insider Knowledge: Painter & Bricklayer",
          "body": "During his political 'wilderness years' out of office, Churchill poured himself into unexpected hobbies. He painted prolifically, producing roughly 550 canvases in his lifetime and writing a charming essay, 'Painting as a Pastime.' He also laid bricks by hand at his country home, Chartwell, building walls and cottages himself. He even joined the Amalgamated Union of Building Trade Workers as a card-carrying bricklayer.",
