        {
          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Insider Knowledge: Empire and the Bengal Famine",
          "body": "An honest portrait of Churchill must reckon with his record on empire. A staunch imperialist, he opposed Indian independence and made disparaging remarks about Indian leaders and people. His government's policies during the 1943 Bengal famine, in which millions died, remain bitterly contested, with critics arguing wartime decisions on grain and shipping worsened the catastrophe. Honoring his leadership against fascism need not erase these darker chapters.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "caption": "A legacy that includes serious moral failings.",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Empire and the Bengal Famine</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"180\" width=\"780\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"228\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A staunch imperialist who opposed</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"262\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Indian independence</text><rect x=\"160\" y=\"330\" width=\"780\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#0d0d1a\" stroke=\"#888\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"25\" fill=\"#888\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1943 Bengal famine: millions died</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"420\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#9ad\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Critics argue wartime grain and shipping</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"450\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"21\" fill=\"#9ad\" text-anchor=\"middle\">decisions worsened the catastrophe</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Honoring his leadership need not</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"638\" font-family=\"Arial, sans-serif\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">erase these darker chapters</text></svg>"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "quote",
          "title": "A Life, Held Whole",
          "content": "Winston Churchill is buried in the churchyard of St Martin's, Bladon, a short walk from Blenheim Palace where he was born ninety years before. The grave is simple — a flat stone shared eventually with Clementine — beside his parents'. The country he had saved continued to argue about him: in schoolbooks, in statues, in television series, in scholarship. Sixty years after his death the argument has grown more sophisticated, not less. He was indispensable in 1940 and culpable in 1943. He was the architect of the welfare state at 33 and the obstacle to Indian self-government at 60. Holding both in one picture is what serious historical thinking now demands. That demand — fair, hard, lasting — is itself the highest tribute a complicated subject can receive.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">A Life, Held Whole</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bladon, Oxfordshire — the quiet end</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"200\" width=\"900\" height=\"760\" fill=\"#2d2d44\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\" rx=\"12\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">\"In war: resolution.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"330\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">In defeat: defiance.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">In victory: magnanimity.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"410\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">In peace: goodwill.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"490\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">— Churchill's \"Moral of the Work,\" WWII memoirs</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"570\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A life that demands a method:</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"620\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read the original speeches; read the Amery diary</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Read Roberts; read Mukerjee</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hold 1940 and 1943 in one judgement</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"740\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Demand of greatness an accounting it can survive</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"820\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">The capstone of the course;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"860\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">the beginning of your own reading.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"930\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\"In life we are reckoned by deeds — not by speeches.\"</text></svg>",
            "caption": "A historical figure who teaches, finally, how to think about historical figures."
          }
        }
